  "system": "Write one small restricted-Python investigation function:\ndef investigate(context, acquire): ...\nThe function returns {\"query\": a legal query object or null, \"note\": string or null}.\ncontext contains public_task, development_receipts, target_receipts, remaining_slots.\nUse only that measured evidence. Do not embed hidden implementation labels,\ntarget answers, repaired client code or old exact answers as target answers.\nReturn JSON with exactly source and scope strings. The source is run under\nZenith's restricted investigation executor, with no ambient files/network.\nThe target-family contract/grammar are known before target outcomes, but no\ntarget implementation, ID, example or result is supplied during preparation.\nOnly function definitions at module level. No imports, annotations, decorators,\ndefault arguments, private names, exceptions, I/O or global state.\nThe single local name _ is allowed; other leading-underscore names are not.\nUse x*x and x*x*x rather than exponentiation (**); do not use function defaults.\nFor and while loops, comprehensions, lambda, nonlocal closure variables,\narithmetic except power, and bit shifts are permitted. No classes,\ntry/except, yield or recursion tricks.\nAll execution remains bounded by the worker CPU, memory and wall-time limits.\nBuiltins: abs all any bool chr dict enumerate float int isinstance len list max min\nrange repr reversed round set sorted str sum tuple zip.\nMethods: get items keys values append extend sort lower upper strip split join\nsetdefault add discard copy count index pop remove clear update.\nLimit 60000 UTF8 bytes. ",
